format 1

# pklith's built-in catalog (src/catalog T2), compiled into `pkli`. Rows are
# seeded from the sibling gates (root R6). A repository's own `.pklith`
# `## checks` row with the same id replaces one of these; a new id extends
# them. Order within a category is the order `pkli lay` lays them (V4).
#
# `nix` is a nixpkgs attribute, or the name of a flake input for tools
# nixpkgs does not ship (microlith, sherd, itok). `-` means hk runs the check
# itself (`hk util`).
#
# rubocop sets GEM_HOME: with none set, RubyGems falls back to the user gem
# dir because the nix store is read-only, and loads whatever native gems a
# different Ruby built there. /nonexistent is only read, never installed to.

## checks
id|category|nix|glob|check|fix|env|msg
trailing-whitespace|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util trailing-whitespace --diff {{files}}|hk util trailing-whitespace --fix {{files}}|-|trailing blanks; the pre-commit hook strips them
final-newline|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util end-of-file-fixer --diff {{files}}|hk util end-of-file-fixer --fix {{files}}|-|file must end with a newline
line-endings|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util mixed-line-ending --diff {{files}}|hk util mixed-line-ending --fix {{files}}|-|file mixes CRLF and LF
no-bom|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util check-byte-order-marker {{files}}|-|-|file starts with a byte order marker
no-merge-conflict|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util check-merge-conflict --assume-in-merge {{files}}|-|-|leftover merge conflict markers
no-case-conflict|hygiene|-|**/*|hk util check-case-conflict {{files}}|-|-|two paths differ only by case
no-broken-symlinks|hygiene|-|-|git ls-files -z \| xargs -0 hk util check-symlinks|-|-|a symlink points nowhere
no-private-key|secret|-|**/*|hk util detect-private-key {{files}}|-|-|a private key block is staged
ripsecrets|secret|ripsecrets|**/*|ripsecrets {{files}}|-|-|a token or credential is staged; a false positive goes in .secretsignore
nixfmt|format|nixfmt|**/*.nix|nixfmt --check {{files}}|nixfmt {{files}}|-|nix file not formatted
shfmt|format|shfmt|**/*.sh, **/*.bash|shfmt --diff {{files}}|shfmt --write {{files}}|-|shell script not formatted
taplo|format|taplo|**/*.toml|taplo fmt --check {{files}}|taplo fmt {{files}}|-|TOML not formatted or not parseable
rustfmt|format|rustfmt|**/*.rs|cargo fmt --check|cargo fmt|-|Rust not formatted
typos|lint|typos|**/*|typos --force-exclude {{files}}|-|-|misspelling; fix it or teach .typos.toml
shellcheck|lint|shellcheck|**/*.sh, **/*.bash, .envrc|shellcheck {{files}}|-|-|shell script finding
clippy|lint|clippy|**/*.rs, Cargo.toml, clippy.toml|cargo clippy --all-targets -q -- -D warnings|-|-|clippy finding
rubocop|lint|rubocop|**/*.rb, **/*.rake, **/*.gemspec, Gemfile, Rakefile|rubocop --force-exclusion {{files}}|rubocop --autocorrect --force-exclusion {{files}}|GEM_HOME=/nonexistent|Ruby style or lint offense
actionlint|lint|actionlint|.github/workflows/*.yml, .github/workflows/*.yaml|actionlint {{files}}|-|-|workflow does not parse or type-check
zizmor|lint|zizmor|.github/workflows/*.yml, .github/workflows/*.yaml|zizmor --offline --no-progress {{files}}|-|-|workflow security finding
statix|lint|statix|**/*.nix|(for f in {{files}}; do statix check "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|(for f in {{files}}; do statix fix "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|-|nix anti-pattern; statix names the lint and its fix
deadnix|lint|deadnix|**/*.nix|deadnix --fail {{files}}|deadnix --edit {{files}}|-|unused nix binding or argument; remove it, or prefix it with _
editorconfig-checker|lint|editorconfig-checker|**/*|editorconfig-checker {{files}}|-|-|file breaks its .editorconfig (indent, line ends, final newline)
mth-fmt|spec|microlith|**/SPEC.md|(for f in {{files}}; do mth fmt --check "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|(for f in {{files}}; do mth fmt "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|-|SPEC.md is hard-wrapped or over the line cap
mth-check|spec|microlith|**/SPEC.md|(for f in {{files}}; do mth check "$f" \|\| exit 1; done)|-|-|SPEC.md breaks a structural rule
sherd-check|spec|sherd|**/SPEC.md, **/*.rs|sherd check|-|-|a citation across spec nodes does not resolve
sherd-nav|spec|sherd|**/SPEC.md|sherd sync --check|sherd sync|-|a §N table is stale
sherd-budget|spec|sherd|**/SPEC.md, .context-limits|sherd budget|-|-|a spec chain is over its ceiling
itok|spec|itok|**/*, .context-limits|itok check|-|-|a file registered in .context-limits is over its token ceiling

# Fragments (catalog §C): which checks a repository gets, from the files it
# tracks. Ported from set-and-setting's detect-fragments.sh and
# check-fragment-map.nix; its order, less the fragments whose checks pklith
# does not ship, plus rust, spec and context. A trigger is a
# glob over tracked paths, matched as hk matches (`*` crosses `/`);
# `always` switches a fragment on in every repository.

## fragments
fragment|triggers|checks|seed
base|always|trailing-whitespace, final-newline, line-endings, no-bom, no-merge-conflict, no-case-conflict, no-broken-symlinks, no-private-key, ripsecrets, typos, editorconfig-checker|-
actions|.github/workflows/*.yml, .github/workflows/*.yaml|actionlint, zizmor|-
nix|**/*.nix|nixfmt, statix, deadnix|-
shell|**/*.sh, **/*.bash|shellcheck, shfmt|-
rubocop|**/.rubocop.yml, **/*.gemspec|rubocop|-
toml|**/*.toml|taplo|-
rust|**/Cargo.toml, **/*.rs|rustfmt, clippy|-
spec|**/SPEC.md|mth-fmt, mth-check, sherd-check, sherd-nav, sherd-budget|-
context|.context-limits|itok|-
